OVERVIEW: Start an embedded JPIP server for local DICOM files

Launches a JPIP server that serves DICOM files from a local directory.
Clients can then use dicom-jpip fetch or any JPIP-compatible viewer.

Examples:
  dicom-jpip serve --directory /path/to/dicoms
  dicom-jpip serve --port 8081 --directory /path/to/dicoms --max-clients 10

USAGE: dicom-jpip serve [--port <port>] [--directory <directory>] [--max-clients <max-clients>] [--client-bandwidth <client-bandwidth>] [--verbose]

OPTIONS:
  -p, --port <port>       Port to listen on (default: 8080) (default: 8080)
  -d, --directory <directory>
                          Directory of DICOM files to serve (default: .)
  --max-clients <max-clients>
                          Maximum concurrent clients (default: 16) (default: 16)
  --client-bandwidth <client-bandwidth>
                          Per-client bandwidth limit in bytes/sec (0 =
                          unlimited) (default: 0)
  -v, --verbose           Verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

